  ('cs_vincennes_history', 'plc_vincennes', 'overview', 'History',
   'Vincennes is a commune in the Val-de-Marne department in the eastern suburbs of Paris, France. It is located 6.7 km (4.2 mi) from the centre of Paris. Vincennes is famous for its castle: the Château de Vincennes. It is next to but does not include the Bois de Vincennes, from which it took its name, which is attached to the city of Paris.', '["clm_wiki_vincennes_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'places_ingest_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
