  ('cs_gaffney_history', 'plc_gaffney', 'overview', 'History',
   'Gaffney is a surname common to the region of Cavan in Ireland, and now spread across other English-speaking nations. Gaffney comes from the Gaelic septs of Ó Gamhna, Mac Conghamhna and Ó Caibheanaigh. Gaffney more commonly does not appear with the Gaelic prefixes of O'' or Mc but there have been Gaffneys recorded with either of the Gaelic prefixes.', '["clm_wiki_gaffney_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'places_ingest_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
