  ('cs_portage_history', 'plc_portage', 'overview', 'History',
   'Portage or portaging is the practice of carrying water craft or cargo over land, either around an obstacle in a river, or between two bodies of water. A path where items are regularly carried between bodies of water is also called a portage. The term comes from French, where porter means "to carry", as in "portable".', '["clm_wiki_portage_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'places_ingest_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
